diff --git a/docs/options.rst b/docs/options.rst
index 39f66c4..00e098e 100644
--- a/docs/options.rst
+++ b/docs/options.rst
@@ -725,6 +725,13 @@ And from the command line:
 In that case it can also be a list of different environment variables
 where the first one is picked.
 
+For a non-boolean flag, any non-empty environment variable value enables
+it and uses its ``flag_value``. For example, an option declared with
+``flag_value='upper'`` and ``envvar='UPPER'`` produces ``'upper'`` when
+``UPPER=1``, just as if the flag was passed on the command line. An empty
+or unset environment variable does not enable the flag. With
+``multiple=True``, it produces a tuple containing one ``flag_value``.
+
 Multiple Values from Environment Values
 ---------------------------------------
 
